  "control": "The same procedure run with the executor of the previous pin, the Ptah v0.22.0 release image, reproduced every checked-in reading record for record, the three PostgreSQL 18 witnesses included, and all four saved exclusion plans byte for byte. The v0.23.0 image reproduced both migration History readings and both restored-history refusals, and changed every schema reading. Each MySQL schema command now asks who the session is and what it holds, with SELECT CURRENT_USER(), VERSION(), SHOW GRANTS and a read of the partial_revokes and lower_case_table_names settings, so that it can refuse a read of what the account cannot see (stokaro/ptah#5545), and it lists the database's events (stokaro/ptah#5552). Each PostgreSQL schema command reads what an object's owner holds apart from its grants (stokaro/ptah#5528), which constraints a table inherits (stokaro/ptah#5529) and the role it runs as (stokaro/ptah#5542). The table, column, index, constraint and view reads of both engines leave out Ptah's seed ledger schema_seeds (stokaro/ptah#5641). The allowed Apply executes the same statements as before. Three saved exclusion plans carry the same statements under new fingerprints and plan names; the wide MySQL plan is unchanged.",
